    "compare_6": {
      "type": "wh-compare",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "choose your friction",
        "body": "<p>The choice between the SP-005 and the CR-005 ultimately comes down to play style, type of game and preference of feel. Both pads are the same tempered glass. What differs is the etch, and what that does at the end of a movement. One surface lets the mouse run, the other gives you something to push against when you stop. The right one depends on whether your aim is built on tracking movements or flicking fast.</p>",
        "color_scheme": "light",
        "spacing": "large"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "compare_item_1": {
          "type": "wh-compare-item",
          "settings": {
            "name": "SP-005",
            "show_tags": true,
            "suitable_label": "suitable for",
            "description": "<p>The faster of the two. A slight texture gives you enough feedback to feel where the mouse is without slowing it down, which puts it in the middle of the range rather than at either extreme. Pick it if you prefer a low-friction, fast mouse gilde.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/wh-compare-surface.jpg",
            "image_fit": "fill",
            "image_background": "solid"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "compare_tag_1": {
              "type": "wh-compare-tag",
              "settings": {
                "label": "tracking-heavy games"
              }
            },
            "compare_tag_2": {
              "type": "wh-compare-tag",
              "settings": {
                "label": "hero shooters"
              }
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "compare_tag_1",
            "compare_tag_2"
          ]
        },
        "compare_item_2": {
          "type": "wh-compare-item",
          "settings": {
            "name": "CR-005",
            "show_tags": true,
            "suitable_label": "suitable for",
            "description": "<p>The control surface. Press harder and it responds, slowing the glide instead of letting the mouse carry past the target. It's the closest thing we make to a cloth pad's stopping power, which makes it the straightforward choice if you're moving over from cloth and don't want to relearn how you aim.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/wh-compare-surface.jpg",
            "image_fit": "fill",
            "image_background": "solid"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "compare_tag_1": {
              "type": "wh-compare-tag",
              "settings": {
                "label": "flick-intensive games"
              }
            },
            "compare_tag_2": {
              "type": "wh-compare-tag",
              "settings": {
                "label": "tactical shooters"
              }
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "compare_tag_1",
            "compare_tag_2"
          ]
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "compare_item_1",
        "compare_item_2"
      ]
    },
    "faq_7": {
      "type": "wh-faq",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "light"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_1": {
          "type": "wh-faq-item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why would I use a glass mousepad?",
            "answer": "<p>Glass mousepads offer truly unparalleled surface experiences and performance, whether you prefer speed or control. While maintaining their quickness for an incredibly long time. Since it’s hardened glass, the consistency of the surface will be unmatched, making it stand the test of time with significantly longer lifespan than cloth.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_2": {
          "type": "wh-faq-item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the surface coated?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The texture is etched into the glass itself, not applied on top. Coatings wear through where you use them most, which is how a pad ends up feeling different in the middle than at the edges. Uncoated glass doesn't do that. What it feels like out of the box is what it feels like in two years</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_3": {
          "type": "wh-faq-item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are glass mousepads fragile?",
            "answer": "<p>Our mousepads are built using tempered glass, making them extremely resistant to cracks, chips and long-term wear. Even though we’ve made the glass thinner for ergonomics, it's stil made of tough, tempered glass. The surface is also stain-proof and immune to issues like edge fraying or humidity damage.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_item_1",
        "faq_item_2",
        "faq_item_3"
      ]
    },
    "text_media_8": {
      "type": "wh-text-media",
      "settings": {
        "no_space_top": false,
        "no_space_bottom": false,
        "show_heading": true,
        "heading": "Spill it, wipe it, keep playing",
        "body": "<p>Glass is non-porous, and so is the silicone under it. Sweat, condensation, a knocked-over drink: none of it soaks in. Cleaning involves just a microfibre cloth and water, or a glass-safe cleaner if something has dried on. No stains, no edge fraying, no soft patches where your palm sits.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/wh-camp-34e00e1d.png",
